In the humid jungles of Stranglethorn Vale, Kipglem Sparkspark, a gnome warlock with goggles askew and a satchel full of unstable vials, crept behind a thicket of thornbushes. His succubus, Lilithra, shimmered beside him—elegant, silent, and *invisible*. She’d cast *Veil of Shadow* moments before, and now they both watched a group of Venture Co. thugs arguing over loot. Kip whispered, “Ready on three.” Lilithra nodded, her eyes glowing faintly in the gloom. *One… two…* With a flick of her wrist, she unleashed *Dominate Mind* on the foreman—*three!* Kip unleashed his imp, then his voidwalker, but Lilithra was already in the fray, her *Seduction* pulling the rest into chaos. They cleaned up in seconds. Kip grinned. “Why do *everyone* say succubi are rare? You’re perfect.” Lilithra smirked. “Because most warlocks forget to train her *first*.”

**Answer:**  
Succubi are *not* commonly used for leveling because their *Seduction* ability is *not* available until level 30—and most players level warlocks solo before then, making the voidwalker (with its *Voidwalker’s Sacrifice* and tanking) far more practical early on. [end of text]


